<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Wittenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1502–1817</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a> was founded in 1502 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-elector-of-saxony">Frederick the Wise</a>, Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, in his residence town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> taught theology there from 1512 and Philip Melanchthon from 1518, making it the intellectual centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Protestant Reformation</a>. It was merged with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-halle">University of Halle</a> in 1817 to form the present Martin Luther University of Halle-Wittenberg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-wittenberg.jpg" alt="University of Wittenberg" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown ; svg from Lumu (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Double_seal_University_of_Halle-Wittenberg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
